  ranking=[2, 5, 3, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31]

[6] Extracted proof/program directions
  1. Use mod-p diagonal-lift infeasibility as a cheap exact irreducibility prefilter before expensive Z-factorization.
  2. Use Newton/valuation hulls for the cases where residue reduction collapses to a reducible shadow, especially Eisenstein/Dumas rows.
  3. Treat the leftover no-small-blocker rows as the proper target for Singh-depth and recombination certificates.
  4. For HYP-2449, replace sign-only chambers by split-survivor signatures: which hidden degree rectangles remain possible?
  5. For LRC14, copy the same split-survivor language: a dangerous residue fiber is one whose local lift survivors never empty.

Conclusion:
  The coefficient row is a diagonal projection of a hidden factor grid.
  Residue blockers empty the possible split set; Newton blockers see
  valuation rigidity when the residue shadow is misleading.  The next
  carrier should track split survivors, not just coefficient signs.
